To find the earliest year of accident data available overall, we need to resolve the "overall" state to an AGS code. We can try using the resolve_region tool to find the correct code.

Here is the revised call:

{"name": "resolve_region", "parameters": {"col": "overall"}}

You can use the `get_accident_trend` function to compare the number of accidents in Bavaria between 2019 and 2022. 

Here's an example of how you can do it:

```bash
{
  "$defs": {
    "Category": {
      "enum": ["fatal", "serious", "light"],
      "title": "Category",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "State": {
      "enum": ["SH", "HH", "NI", "HB", "NW", "HE", "RP", "BW", "BY", "SL", "BE", "BB", "MV", "SN", "ST", "TH"],
      "title": "State",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "state": "BA",
  "category": "fatal",
  "year": [2019, 2022]
}
```

This will return the number of fatal accidents in Bavaria for the years 2019 and 2022.

If you want to compare the number of accidents in all severities, you can omit the `category` parameter.

```bash
{
  "$defs": {
    "Category": {
      "enum": ["fatal", "serious", "light"],
      "title": "Category",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "State": {
